Subject: winebuild,gdi32,user32: emit traditional x86 hotpatch prologues for Clang i386 DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH APIs
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later

When building i386 PE modules with llvm-mingw (Clang + LLD), -fms-hotpatch emits
a two-byte 66 90 NOP at function entry while LLD's --functionpadmin fills the
preceding inter-section padding with 0xcc. Older Windows hotpatchers (such as
rUGP localization hooks) require five 0x90 NOP bytes before the entry point and
an 8b ff (mov edi, edi) two-byte entry instruction.

Map DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH on Clang i386 to __patchable_function_entry__(8, 6) and
__noinline__ so each hotpatchable function owns six 0x90 bytes before its
two-byte-aligned entry and intra-DLL wrappers do not inline it. In winebuild's
make_builtin_files pass, rewrite the 66 90 entry of i386 functions preceded by
five 0x90 bytes to 8b ff. Mark CreateFontIndirectA, GetGlyphOutlineA,
EnumFontFamiliesExA, and AppendMenuA with DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH alongside the
existing CreateWindowExA and SetWindowTextA annotations.

